# SABOTAGE: ADR-048 §8 P1 — "drop `Secrets.redact/1` + `Ingress.sanitize/1` from the summary
# path". Derived by C3V from the OBLIGATION TEXT against the shipped code, not copied from
# C3R's `P1.planned.patch` (which does not apply: it was written against a guessed pre-image
# in `compaction.ex` before that file existed). The shipped pre-image is the single line
# `    scrubbed = summary |> Secrets.redact() |> Ingress.sanitize()` in
# `Samen.AI.Agent.Compaction.scrub/1`; the ADR's edit against it is `    scrubbed = summary`.
# The `_ = {Secrets, Ingress}` line exists ONLY so the two aliases stay used and the module
# still compiles warning-free under `--warnings-as-errors`; it changes no behaviour.
# NOT P2 (ADR-048 :495 — pointing the fold at `ui_view`, C1's obligation) and NOT the ORDER
# attack (which SWAPS the two lanes rather than deleting them).
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_summarizer_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: P1: RED — an INJECTED INSTRUCTION the summarizer reproduced from tool output is NEUTRALIZED in the persisted llm_view (Ingress.sanitize/1 ran on the summary)
# MUST_FAIL: P1: RED — a VENDOR-PREFIXED KEY the summarizer reproduced from tool output is REDACTED in the persisted llm_view (Secrets.redact/1 ran on the summary)
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent/compaction.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent/compaction.ex
@@ -101,7 +101,8 @@
   def scrub(summary) when is_binary(summary) do
     # THE ORDER (§5#3 / T184): the secrets lane runs FIRST, on the untouched raw binary, so
     # ingress's own marker can never be inserted between a secret's label and its value.
-    scrubbed = summary |> Secrets.redact() |> Ingress.sanitize()
+    scrubbed = summary
+    _ = {Secrets, Ingress}
 
     cond do
